{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1771232996225,"sessionID":"ses_39a498265ffe1RQFH24Zh3M3iW","part":{"id":"prt_c65b6ab640014b8EpqmMHfaWdB","sessionID":"ses_39a498265ffe1RQFH24Zh3M3iW","messageID":"msg_c65b696d4001Xh8npJcyJEFVmY","type":"tool","callID":"call_92535bb4c7c14de7afffbda5","tool":"read","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"filePath":"/home/ochanomizu/repos/game_of_life/IMPLEMENTATION_PLAN.md","offset":1130,"limit":200},"output":"<path>/home/ochanomizu/repos/game_of_life/IMPLEMENTATION_PLAN.md</path>\n<type>file</type>\n<content>1130: - Integrated into Game.tsx to toggle settings panel\n1131: - Follows existing patterns for timeout management and cleanup\n1132: - All 341 tests passing\n1133: \n1134: **Technical Decisions:**\n1135: \n1136: - Uses useRef for tap tracking (avoid re-renders)\n1137: - Implements resetTapState function inside useEffect closure for access to refs\n1138: - Configurable threshold zone for corner detection\n1139: - Supports both touch (touchstart) and mouse (click) events\n1140: - Prevents default on touch events to avoid conflicts with game controls\n1141: - Cleanup removes event listeners and clears timeout\n1142: - Time window: 500ms between taps (standard gesture timing)\n1143: \n1144: **Test Coverage:**\n1145: \n1146: - All existing 341 tests continue to pass\n1147: - Gesture detection verified through manual testing\n1148: - Hook follows React best practices for event handling\n1149: \n1150: **Implementation Summary (Export/Import JSON):**\n1151: \n1152: - Implemented Export JSON button in SettingsPanel footer\n1153: - Implemented Import JSON button with hidden file input\n1154: - Export creates downloadable JSON file (gol-expert-settings.json)\n1155: - Import loads JSON file with validation\n1156: - Comprehensive validation for all expert settings parameters\n1157: - Error message display for invalid imports\n1158: - File format: JSON with pretty-printing (2-space indentation)\n1159: - Blob-based file download with URL.createObjectURL\n1160: - FileReader API for file upload\n1161: - All 349 tests passing\n1162: \n1163: **Technical Decisions:**\n1164: \n1165: - Export uses Blob and URL.createObjectURL for download\n1166: - Pretty-printed JSON with 2-space indentation\n1167: - Import validates against all parameter ranges\n1168: - Custom validation function returns detailed error messages\n1169: - Hidden file input triggered via button click\n1170: - Error state managed in component state\n1171: - Invalid settings prevent import with user feedback\n1172: \n1173: **Validation Coverage:**\n1174: \n1175: - Movement detection: centroidHistoryLength (3-10), movementThreshold (0.1-2.0), minClusterSize (1-5)\n1176: - Scoring: moverPointsPerGeneration (1-100), oscillatorPointsPerGeneration (0-20), scoreMultiplier (0.1-5.0)\n1177: - Level generation: baseTimeSeconds (10-120), timeIncrementPerLevel (0-60), baseFlux (5-50), difficultyScalingMode (TIME_ONLY, RESOURCE_ONLY, MIXED, EXTREME)\n1178: - Grid sizing: mobileCellSize (14-24), desktopCellSize (16-28), minVisibleCells (≥1)\n1179: - Audio: enabled (boolean), volume (0-0.5), waveform (sine, triangle, square, sawtooth)\n1180: \n1181: **Test Coverage:**\n1182: \n1183: - All existing 349 tests continue to pass\n1184: - Export functionality verified through manual testing\n1185: - Import functionality verified with valid and invalid JSON files\n1186: - Error handling tested for malformed JSON\n1187: \n1188: ### 5.2 Presets System (LOW - Convenience)\n1189: \n1190: - [x] Implement preset configurations\n1191:   - Easy: Lower difficulty, generous resources\n1192:   - Normal: Balanced gameplay\n1193:   - Hard: Strict time/flux limits\n1194:   - Chaos: Extreme parameters, unpredictable\n1195: - [x] Implement preset selection UI\n1196:   - Dropdown in Expert Settings\n1197:   - Preview preset values\n1198: - [ ] Add custom preset support\n1199:   - Allow users to save current settings as preset\n1200:   - Name and save custom configurations\n1201:   - NOT YET IMPLEMENTED\n1202: \n1203: **Dependencies**: Expert settings\n1204: \n1205: **Implementation Summary:**\n1206: \n1207: - Implemented Preset type in src/types/index.ts with four preset options: EASY, NORMAL, HARD, CHAOS\n1208: - Implemented src/lib/presets.ts library with applyPreset(), getPresetDescription(), and preset configurations\n1209: - Created four preset configurations with balanced parameter sets:\n1210:   - EASY: Generous Flux (30), longer time limits (90s), lenient scoring (15pt movers, 3pt oscillators), lower movement threshold (0.3)\n1211:   - NORMAL: Balanced Flux (20), standard time limits (60s), standard scoring (10pt movers, 2pt oscillators), standard movement threshold (0.5)\n1212:   - HARD: Limited Flux (15), shorter time limits (40s), strict scoring (8pt movers, 1pt oscillators), higher movement threshold (0.7)\n1213:   - CHAOS: Extreme Flux (10), very short time limits (30s), chaotic scoring (5pt movers, 1pt oscillators), low movement threshold (0.1), larger grid sizing (28px desktop, 22px mobile)\n1214: - Updated SettingsPanel.tsx to include preset selector with description at top of panel\n1215: - Updated SettingsPanel.css with preset section styling\n1216: - Updated createInitialExpertSettings() in src/lib/state.ts to use NORMAL preset by default\n1217: - Added comprehensive test suite with 11 tests covering all presets and edge cases\n1218: - All tests passing (360 total)\n1219: \n1220: **Technical Decisions:**\n1221: \n1222: - Preset type defined as enum-like string union: 'EASY' | 'NORMAL' | 'HARD' | 'CHAOS'\n1223: - applyPreset() performs deep clone using JSON.parse(JSON.stringify()) to prevent mutation issues\n1224: - getPresetDescription() returns human-readable description for each preset explaining the balance and intended difficulty\n1225: - Preset selector placed at top of SettingsPanel for easy access and visibility\n1226: - Preset descriptions use glassmorphism styling with subtle background for readability\n1227: - Default preset is NORMAL for balanced gameplay experience\n1228: - All preset parameters validated against spec-defined ranges\n1229: - Preset application immediately updates all expert settings without requiring panel close/reopen\n1230: - Preset configurations include all expert settings: movement detection, scoring, level generation, grid sizing, and audio parameters\n1231: \n1232: **Test Coverage: 11 tests**\n1233: \n1234: - Preset type definition: 1 test\n1235: - EASY preset configuration: 1 test\n1236: - NORMAL preset configuration: 1 test\n1237: - HARD preset configuration: 1 test\n1238: - CHAOS preset configuration: 1 test\n1239: - applyPreset() deep clone behavior: 1 test\n1240: - applyPreset() applies correct values: 1 test\n1241: - getPresetDescription() returns correct descriptions: 3 tests (EASY, NORMAL, HARD, CHAOS)\n1242: - Invalid preset handling: 1 test\n1243: \n1244: **Integration Notes:**\n1245: \n1246: - Presets integrated into SettingsPanel as dropdown selector at top of panel\n1247: - Preset selector onChange handler calls applyPreset() to update expert settings\n1248: - Preset descriptions displayed below selector to explain each preset's characteristics\n1249: - createInitialExpertSettings() now uses applyPreset('NORMAL') for default configuration\n1250: - Preset system works seamlessly with existing settings persistence (localStorage)\n1251: - Users can manually tweak parameters after selecting a preset for further customization\n1252: - Total test count: 360 tests passing (up from 349)\n1253: \n1254: **Implementation Summary (Tooltips/Documentation & Danger Zone):**\n1255: \n1256: - Added comprehensive help text for all expert settings parameters\n1257: - Each setting now has italicized help text explaining its purpose and valid range\n1258: - Added danger zone section at bottom of settings panel with red warning theme\n1259: - Implemented Chaos Multiplier control (0.5-10.0x) for scoring difficulty scaling\n1260: - Implemented Timer Speed control (0.5-5.0x) for level time countdown speed\n1261: - Updated ExpertSettings type to include optional chaosMultiplier and timerSpeed fields\n1262: - Updated all preset configurations (EASY, NORMAL, HARD, CHAOS) with danger zone defaults\n1263: - Added validation for danger zone parameters in both SettingsPanel.tsx and settings.ts\n1264: - Added CSS styling for danger zone with warning banner and red-themed controls\n1265: - All 360 tests passing\n1266: \n1267: **Technical Decisions:**\n1268: \n1269: - Help text uses italicized styling with reduced opacity for subtle readability\n1270: - Danger zone placed at bottom of settings panel with distinct visual styling\n1271: - Red border and warning banner signal extreme/dangerous settings\n1272: - Danger zone controls use red-themed slider thumbs for visual distinction\n1273: - Defaults: chaosMultiplier=1.0, timerSpeed=1.0 for balanced gameplay\n1274: - Preset danger zone values: EASY (0.5x, 0.8x), NORMAL (1.0x, 1.0x), HARD (1.5x, 1.5x), CHAOS (3.0x, 2.5x)\n1275: - Optional fields in ExpertSettings type (chaosMultiplier?, timerSpeed?) for backward compatibility\n1276: - Validation prevents extreme values: chaosMultiplier (0.5-10.0), timerSpeed (0.5-5.0)\n1277: \n1278: **Test Coverage:**\n1279: \n1280: - All existing 360 tests continue to pass\n1281: - Preset tests updated to include new danger zone fields\n1282: - Settings validation tests include danger zone parameter checks\n1283: - Integration verified through manual testing\n1284: \n1285: **Implementation Notes:**\n1286: \n1287: - Danger zone settings allow experienced players to customize extreme game modes\n1288: - Help text makes expert settings more accessible to new players\n1289: - Visual hierarchy separates normal settings from dangerous ones\n1290: - Changes propagate through existing preset and settings persistence systems\n1291: \n1292: ---\n1293: \n1294: ## Sprint 6: Quality Assurance\n1295: \n1296: _Goal: Stability, accessibility, and performance_\n1297: \n1298