ariable from catch block to satisfy ESLint no-unused-vars rule\n1590: - Fixed synchronous setState warnings in React effects:\n1591:   - FluxDisplay: wrapped setState in useCallback with proper dependency tracking\n1592:   - ScoreDisplay: wrapped setState in useCallback with proper dependency tracking\n1593:   - Game: refactored levelStats from state to computed value using useMemo\n1594: - Added eslint rule override for test files to allow 'any' types when needed for test doubles\n1595: \n1596: **Technical Decisions:**\n1597: \n1598: - Used window.clearTimeout to ensure global recognition across all environments\n1599: - Created separate vitest.config.ts to isolate test environment configuration from production build\n1600: - Record<string, unknown> provides better type safety than 'any' while maintaining flexibility\n1601: - useMemo for levelStats prevents unnecessary re-computation and state updates\n1602: - useCallback for setState functions ensures stable references across renders\n1603: - ESLint overrides for test files scoped to .test.ts and .spec.ts extensions only\n1604: \n1605: **Verification Results:**\n1606: \n1607: - All 360 tests passing\n1608: - Build successful (npm run build)\n1609: - TypeScript compilation clean (npm run typecheck)\n1610: - ESLint passing (npm run lint)\n1611: - Git tag 0.1.5 created and pushed\n1612: \n1613: ---\n1614: \n1615: ## Parallel Development Tracks\n1616: \n1617: ### Track A (Can start after Project Setup):\n1618: \n1619: - Type definitions → Shared utilities → All other systems\n1620: \n1621: ### Track B (Can start after Simulation Engine):\n1622: \n1623: - Phase Management → UI Overlay → Phase Status Display\n1624: - Canvas Rendering → Grid Interaction\n1625: \n1626: ### Track C (Can start after Simulation Engine):\n1627: \n1628: - User Interaction → Audio Sonification → Visual Polish\n1629: - Flux Management → Grid Interaction\n1630: \n1631: ### Track D (Can start after Canvas Rendering + User Interaction + Flux Management):\n1632: \n1633: - Grid Integration → Playable MVP\n1634: \n1635: ### Track E (Can start after MVP):\n1636: \n1637: - Intro Overlay → Main UI Controls → Settings Panel\n1638: - Movement Detection → Scoring System → Level Progression\n1639: \n1640: ### Track F (Can start after Level Progression):\n1641: \n1642: - Transition System → Victory Screen\n1643: \n1644: ### Track G (Can start after Scoring + Level Progression):\n1645: \n1646: - Audio Sonification → Visual Polish → Mobile Enhancements\n1647: \n1648: ### Track H (Can start after all features):\n1649: \n1650: - Expert Settings → Presets → Error Handling → Accessibility → Performance → Testing → Documentation\n1651: \n1652: ---\n1653: \n1654: ## Critical Path (Sequential Must-Haves for MVP):\n1655: \n1656: 1. **Project Setup** → Build system\n1657: 2. **Type Definitions** → All type-safe development\n1658: 3. **Shared Utilities** → Validation and state management\n1659: 4. **Simulation Engine** → Core gameplay logic\n1660: 5. **Phase Management with COUNTDOWN** → Game flow control\n1661: 6. **Canvas Rendering** → Visual feedback\n1662: 7. **User Interaction** → Input handling\n1663: 8. **Flux Management** → Resource system\n1664: 9. **Grid Integration** → Playable MVP\n1665: \n1666: ## Testing Milestones:\n1667: \n1668: - **After Sprint 1**: MVP manually playable (place cells, watch simulation, all phases work)\n1669: - **After Sprint 2**: Full game UI (intro, controls, scoring, settings)\n1670: - **After Sprint 3**: Complete game loop (intro → levels → transitions → victory)\n1671: - **After Sprint 4**: Audio and polish (all sounds, visual enhancements, mobile support)\n1672: - **After Sprint 5**: Expert settings and customization\n1673: - **After Sprint 6**: Production-ready with stability, accessibility, performance, tests, and docs\n1674: \n1675: ## Success Criteria:\n1676: \n1677: - [ ] Playable MVP after Sprint 1 (can place cells and run simulation with all phases)\n1678: - [ ] Complete UI after Sprint 2 (intro, controls, settings)\n1679: - [ ] Full game loop after Sprint 3 (intro → levels → scoring → transitions → victory)\n1680: - [ ] Audio and polish after Sprint 4 (all sounds, animations, mobile support)\n1681: - [ ] All features implemented after Sprint 5 (expert settings, presets)\n1682: - [ ] Production-ready after Sprint 6 (stability, accessibility, performance, tests, docs)\n1683: - [ ] 60fps performance with 500+ cells\n1684: - [ ] Works on mobile and desktop\n1685: - [ ] Audio works across all major browsers\n1686: - [ ] No console errors or warnings in production\n1687: - [ ] High score persistence works\n1688: - [ ] Expert settings properly configure all systems\n1689: - [ ] All critical edge cases handled gracefully\n1690: - [ ] Accessible keyboard navigation\n1691: - [ ] Comprehensive test coverage for core systems\n1692: - [ ] Clear documentation for developers and players\n1693: \n1694: ## Framework Decisions (MAKE THESE FIRST):\n1695: \n1696: - **Framework**: React/Vite (recommended for performance and DX)\n1697: - **State Management**: React hooks (useState, useReducer, useRef) - minimal, no external library needed\n1698: - **Styling**: CSS modules or vanilla CSS with CSS variables for theming\n1699: - **Testing**: Vitest (fast, compatible with Vite)\n1700: - **Build Tool**: Vite (recommended for speed and simplicity)\n1701: \n1702: ## Implementation Order Recommendations:\n1703: \n1704: ### Week 1: Foundation\n1705: \n1706: 1. Project setup (Day 1)\n1707: 2. Type definitions (Day 1)\n1708: 3. Shared utilities (Day 2)\n1709: 4. Simulation engine (Day 2-3)\n1710: 5. Phase management with COUNTDOWN (Day 3-4)\n1711: 6. Canvas rendering (Day 4)\n1712: \n1713: ### Week 2: Interaction & UI\n1714: \n1715: 7. User interaction (Day 1)\n1716: 8. Flux management (Day 1-2)\n1717: 9. Grid interaction (Day 2) - MVP milestone reached\n1718: 10. Intro overlay (Day 3)\n1719: 11. Main UI controls (Day 3-4)\n1720: 12. Phase status display (Day 4)\n1721: \n1722: 