{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1771233228780,"sessionID":"ses_39a498265ffe1RQFH24Zh3M3iW","part":{"id":"prt_c65b9a69e001b0jBmEL5s6oGz1","sessionID":"ses_39a498265ffe1RQFH24Zh3M3iW","messageID":"msg_c65b8e3dd001sjt0S18svT5XWa","type":"tool","callID":"call_b5888e06f6bd458cb274879a","tool":"task","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"description":"Check current test status","prompt":"Run the test suite to verify current test status. Execute `npm run test:run` in /home/ochanomizu/repos/game_of_life and capture the results. Return:\n1. Total number of tests\n2. Number of passing tests\n3. Number of failing tests\n4. Any error messages or warnings\n5. Overall test suite health","subagent_type":"general"},"output":"task_id: ses_39a465952ffediODOCS0n58HIr (for resuming to continue this task if needed)\n\n<task_result>\n## Test Suite Results\n\n**Total tests:** 374  \n**Passing tests:** 374  \n**Failing tests:** 0\n\n**Warnings/Errors:**\n- Multiple `HTMLCanvasElement's getContext() not implemented` warnings (canvas npm package not installed)\n- `navigation to another Document` not implemented warning  \n- localStorage error warnings in `src/lib/state.test.ts` (expected test behavior)\n- `IntroOverlay` update not wrapped in `act(...)` warning in `src/lib/IntroOverlay.test.tsx`\n- `vi.fn()` mock implementation warning in `src/lib/audio.test.ts`\n- AudioContext constructor error (test still passed)\n- Invalid level number warnings in `src/lib/level.test.ts` (expected validation behavior)\n\n**Overall health:** ✅ All tests passing. Suite is healthy but has non-critical warnings that could be addressed for better test quality.\n</task_result>","title":"Check current test status","metadata":{"sessionId":"ses_39a465952ffediODOCS0n58HIr","model":{"modelID":"glm-4.7","providerID":"zai-coding-plan"},"truncated":false},"time":{"start":1771233191595,"end":1771233228778}}}}
{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1771233283653,"sessionID":"ses_39a498265ffe1RQFH24Zh3M3iW","part":{"id":"prt_c65b9a66e001oUZS6dboo0AT8X","sessionID":"ses_39a498265ffe1RQFH24Zh3M3iW","messageID":"msg_c65b8e3dd001sjt0S18svT5XWa","type":"tool","callID":"call_0d7251562c63466dbb864cd0","tool":"task","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"description":"Verify custom preset support","prompt":"Search /home/ochanomizu/repos/game_of_life/src for custom preset functionality in the expert settings. Look for:\n1. Ability to save current settings as custom preset\n2. UI for naming custom presets\n3. Storage of custom presets\n4. Loading of custom presets\n5. Any preset-related code beyond the built-in EASY, NORMAL, HARD, CHAOS presets\n\nReturn findings about what custom preset features are implemented and what's missing.","subagent_type":"explore"},"output":"task_id: ses_39a46597effemyT9Uzl1t6e5bq (for resuming to continue this task if needed)\n\n<task_result>\nBased on my comprehensive search of the `/home/ochanomizu/repos/game_of_life/src` directory, here are my findings about custom preset functionality in the expert settings:\n\n## Current Preset Implementation\n\n### What Exists (Built-in Presets Only)\n\n1. **Four Hardcoded Presets** (`/home/ochanomizu/repos/game_of_life/src/lib/presets.ts`)\n   - EASY - Generous resources and time limits\n   - NORMAL - Balanced gameplay for standard challenge\n   - HARD - Strict resources and shorter time limits\n   - CHAOS - Extreme settings with rapid changes\n\n2. **Preset Type Definition** (`/home/ochanomizu/repos/game_of_life/src/types/index.ts` line 103)\n   ```typescript\n   export type Preset = 'EASY' | 'NORMAL' | 'HARD' | 'CHAOS'\n   ```\n\n3. **Core Functions** (`/home/ochanomizu/repos/game_of_life/src/lib/presets.ts`)\n   - `applyPreset(preset: Preset)` - Applies a built-in preset\n   - `getPresetName(preset: Preset)` - Returns display name\n   - `getPresetDescription(preset: Preset)` - Returns description\n\n4. **UI Component** (`/home/ochanomizu/repos/game_of_life/src/components/SettingsPanel.tsx` lines 295-317)\n   - Dropdown select with 4 options\n   - Displays preset description below dropdown\n   - Only displays built-in presets\n\n5. **Settings Storage** (`/home/ochanomizu/repos/game_of_life/src/components/Game.tsx`)\n   - Expert settings saved to localStorage with key `'gol-expert-settings'`\n   - Only saves current active settings, not presets\n\n## Custom Preset Features - Status\n\n### 1. Ability to Save Current Settings as Custom Preset\n**NOT IMPLEMENTED** - No function exists to save current settings as a named custom preset\n\n### 2. UI for Naming Custom Presets\n**NOT IMPLEMENTED** - No input field or modal for entering preset names\n\n### 3. Storage of Custom Presets\n**NOT IMPLEMENTED** - No localStorage keys or database for storing custom preset collections\n\n### 4. Loading of Custom Presets\n**NOT IMPLEMENTED** - The preset dropdown only includes the 4 built-in options; custom presets cannot be selected\n\n### 5. Preset-related Code Beyond Built-in Presets\n**NOT IMPLEMENTED** - The entire preset system is limited to the 4 hardcoded presets. There is no:\n   - Dynamic preset management\n   - Preset creation/deletion\n   - User-defined preset extensions\n   - Preset listing or browsing beyond built-in ones\n\n## Summary\n\nThe current implementation provides only the 4 built-in difficulty presets (EASY, NORMAL, HARD, CHAOS) with no infrastructure for custom presets. To add custom preset functionality, the following would need to be implemented:\n\n1. Extend the `Preset` type to allow custom string values\n2. Add functions: `saveCustomPreset(name, settings)`, `loadCustomPreset(name)`, `listCustomPresets()`, `deleteCustomPreset(name)`\n3. Add UI for creating, naming, selecting, and deleting custom presets\n4. Implement storage mechanism (likely localStorage) for custom preset collections\n5. Modify the preset dropdown to dynamically include custom presets\n</task_result>