{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1771233289983,"sessionID":"ses_39a498265ffe1RQFH24Zh3M3iW","part":{"id":"prt_c65b9a65d001m5KwCKphEuj9tA","sessionID":"ses_39a498265ffe1RQFH24Zh3M3iW","messageID":"msg_c65b8e3dd001sjt0S18svT5XWa","type":"tool","callID":"call_d5530ba15de84aae8ea99737","tool":"task","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"description":"Verify performance optimization","prompt":"Search /home/ochanomizu/repos/game_of_life/src for performance optimization features. Look for:\n1. FPS counter (development only)\n2. Memory usage tracking\n3. Component render profiling\n4. Memoization of expensive calculations\n5. Lazy loading of components\n6. Code splitting for production\n7. Performance monitoring code\n\nReturn findings about what performance optimization features are implemented and what's missing.","subagent_type":"explore"},"output":"task_id: ses_39a465995ffePa041sYKuhlYb0 (for resuming to continue this task if needed)\n\n<task_result>\nBased on my thorough search of the `/home/ochanomizu/repos/game_of_life/src` directory, here's my comprehensive report on performance optimization features:\n\n## Performance Optimization Features Analysis\n\n### 1. FPS Counter (Development Only) - **NOT IMPLEMENTED**\nNo FPS counter implementation was found in the codebase. There's no development-only FPS display or monitoring component.\n\n---\n\n### 2. Memory Usage Tracking - **NOT IMPLEMENTED**\nNo memory usage tracking was found. The codebase doesn't use `performance.memory`, `HeapSnapshot`, or any other memory monitoring APIs.\n\n---\n\n### 3. Component Render Profiling - **NOT IMPLEMENTED**\n- No usage of `React.Profiler` component found\n- No `React.memo` usage found in any components\n- No development tool integration for render profiling\n\n---\n\n### 4. Memoization of Expensive Calculations - **PARTIALLY IMPLEMENTED**\n\n**Found in `/src/components/Game.tsx`:**\n- `useMemo` for `levelStats` calculation (line 185-206)\n- `useCallback` extensively used for event handlers (12 instances):\n  - `handleInteractionSound` (line 76)\n  - `handleTransitionSound` (line 80)\n  - `handleFluxErrorSound` (line 84)\n  - `onTripleTap` (line 118)\n  - `handleTransitionComplete` (line 136)\n  - `hasCells` (line 179)\n  - `handleSimulationStep` (line 243)\n  - `handleStart` (line 306)\n  - `handleGridChange` (line 313)\n  - `handleFluxChange` (line 318)\n  - `handleClear` (line 322)\n  - `handleRandom` (line 331)\n  - `handleToggleSettings` (line 353)\n  - `handleUpdateSettings` (line 357)\n  - `handleStep` (line 362)\n\n**Found in other components:**\n- `CanvasGrid.tsx`: `useCallback` for `draw` function (line 51)\n- `GridInteraction.tsx`: 6 `useCallback` hooks for event handlers\n- `useTransition.ts`: 2 `useCallback` hooks for transition handling\n- `usePhaseTimer.ts`: 4 `useCallback` hooks for timer operations\n\n**Total:** 37 instances of `useMemo`/`useCallback` usage across the codebase\n\n---\n\n### 5. Lazy Loading of Components - **NOT IMPLEMENTED**\n- No `React.lazy()` usage found\n- No `React.Suspense` usage found\n- No dynamic imports (`import()`) found in component code\n\n---\n\n### 6. Code Splitting for Production - **NOT IMPLEMENTED**\n\n**Found in `vite.config.ts`:**\n- Minimal Vite configuration with no code splitting setup\n- No manual chunk splitting configuration\n- No dynamic import-based code splitting\n\n---\n\n### 7. Performance Monitoring Code - **PARTIALLY IMPLEMENTED**\n\n**Feature Detection (`/src/lib/featureDetection.ts`):**\n- Checks for `requestAnimationFrame` support (line 19)\n- Checks for `performance.now()` support (line 20)\n- Logs unsupported features via logger (lines 54-67)\n\n**Animation & Timing API Usage:**\n- `performance.now()` used for animation timing:\n  - `CanvasGrid.tsx` (line 96)\n  - `ScoreDisplay.tsx` (line 75)\n  - `FluxDisplay.tsx` (line 42)\n  - `GridInteraction.tsx` (lines 63, 82, 106)\n- `requestAnimationFrame()` for smooth animations:\n  - `Game.tsx` (lines 127, 237)\n  - `CanvasGrid.tsx` (line 196)\n  - `ScoreDisplay.tsx` (line 91, 97)\n  - `FluxDisplay.tsx` (line 53, 60)\n\n**Proper Cleanup:**\n- `cancelAnimationFrame()` usage in:\n  - `CanvasGrid.tsx` (line 204)\n  - `FluxDisplay.tsx` (lines 38, 64)\n- `clearInterval()` usage for timer cleanup:\n  - `Game.tsx` (line 301)\n  - `usePhaseTimer.ts` (lines 21, 39, 88, 102)\n\n**Visibility API Support:**\n- Page Visibility API detected and used (featureDetection.ts line 22)\n- Visibility change handlers in:\n  - `useTransition.ts` (line 137-167)\n  - `usePhaseTimer.ts` (line 35-65)\n\n**Custom Logger (`/src/lib/logger.ts`):**\n- Logging utility with debug, info, warn, and error levels\n- Used throughout the codebase for development feedback\n\n**Missing Features:**\n- No actual FPS measurement/metrics collection\n- No performance marks/measures (performance.mark, performance.measure)\n- No Web Vitals tracking\n- No runtime performance dashboard\n\n---\n\n## Summary Table\n\n| Feature | Status | Details |\n|---------|--------|---------|\n| FPS Counter (dev only) | ❌ Not Implemented | No FPS display or monitoring |\n| Memory Usage Tracking | ❌ Not Implemented | No memory profiling APIs used |\n| Component Render Profiling | ❌ Not Implemented | No React.Profiler or React.memo |\n| Memoization | ⚠️ Partially Implemented | 37 useCallback/useMemo instances |\n| Lazy Loading | ❌ Not Implemented | No React.lazy or Suspense |\n| Code Splitting | ❌ Not Implemented | Minimal Vite config, no splitting |\n| Performance Monitoring | ⚠️ Partially Implemented | Feature detection, timing APIs, cleanup |\n\n## Recommendations\n\n**Missing Critical Performance Features:**\n1. Implement FPS counter for development (can use `requestAnimationFrame` delta)\n2. Add React.memo to expensive components (SettingsPanel, GlassHUD, CanvasGrid)\n3. Consider lazy loading for overlay components (VictoryScreen, SettingsPanel)\n4. Implement code splitting for production builds\n5. Add React.Profiler for render optimization analysis\n6. Consider adding Web Vitals tracking for production monitoring\n\n**Existing Good Practices:**\n1. Proper animation frame cleanup\n2. Visibility API handling for background tabs\n3. useCallback for event handlers to prevent unnecessary re-renders\n4. Feature detection for browser capabilities\n</task_result>","title":"Verify performance optimization","metadata":{"sessionId":"ses_39a465995ffePa041sYKuhlYb0","model":{"modelID":"glm-4.7","providerID":"zai-coding-plan"},"truncated":false},"time":{"start":1771233191528,"end":1771233289981}}}}
{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1771233327176,"sessionID":"ses_39a498265ffe1RQFH24Zh3M3iW","part":{"id":"prt_c65b9a6380010NNVrAd0ASvDNk","sessionID":"ses_39a498265ffe1RQFH24Zh3M3iW","messageID":"msg_c65b8e3dd001sjt0S18svT5XWa","type":"tool","callID":"call_bb63cc992cd24540985ffaa5","tool":"task","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"description":"Verify retry mechanisms implementation","prompt":"Search /home/ochanomizu/repos/game_of_life/src for any implementation of retry mechanisms with exponential backoff. Look for:\n1. Functions that retry failed operations\n2. Exponential backoff logic\n3. Graceful degradation patterns\n4. Any retry-related code in error handling\n\nReturn findings about what retry mechanisms are implemented and what's missing.","subagent_type":"explore"},"output":"task_id: ses_39a4659c2ffegiKCOwIUmDuvIk (for resuming to continue this task if needed)\n\n<task_result>\nBased on my thorough search of the `/home/ochanomizu/repos/game_of_life/src` directory, here are my findings regarding retry mechanisms with exponential backoff:\n\n## Summary\n\n**No robust retry mechanisms with exponential backoff are implemented in this codebase.**\n\n---\n\n## What IS Implemented\n\n### 1. Simple Single Retry for localStorage (src/lib/state.ts, lines 99-121)\n\n**File:** `/home/ochanomizu/repos/game_of_life/src/lib/state.ts`\n\n```typescript\nexport function saveToLocalStorage<T>(key: string, value: T): boolean {\n  const fullKey = `${STORAGE_KEY_PREFIX}${key}`\n  const serialized = JSON.stringify(value)\n\n  try {\n    localStorage.setItem(fullKey, serialized)\n    return true\n  } catch (error) {\n    if (error instanceof DOMException && error.name === 'QuotaExceededError') {\n      console.error('localStorage quota exceeded. Attempting cleanup...')\n      cleanupOldLocalStorageData()\n      try {\n        localStorage.setItem(fullKey, serialized)\n        return true\n      } catch (retryError) {\n        console.error('Failed to save to localStorage after cleanup:', retryError)\n        return false\n      }\n    }\n    console.error('Failed to save to localStorage:', error)\n    return false\n  }\n}\n```\n\n**Characteristics:**\n- Type: Single retry attempt after quota exceeded error\n- Recovery strategy: Clean up old data, then retry\n- No delay between attempts\n- No exponential backoff\n- No configurable retry limits\n- Hardcoded to only one retry\n\n### 2. Graceful Degradation Patterns (No Retry)\n\n#### a. ErrorBoundary Component (src/components/ErrorBoundary.tsx)\n- Catches all React errors and displays error UI\n- Provides page reload functionality\n- Does NOT retry failed operations\n- Full application restart required\n\n#### b. Audio Error Handling (src/lib/audio.ts)\n- Multiple sound playback functions with try-catch blocks (lines 42-246)\n- Logs errors but does NOT retry failed audio operations\n- No retry for AudioContext creation failures\n- Silent failure pattern\n\n#### c. Feature Detection (src/lib/featureDetection.ts)\n- Detects browser feature support (lines 27-52)\n- Gracefully handles missing features\n- No retry mechanism\n\n#### d. localStorage High Scores (src/lib/level.ts)\n```typescript\nfunction loadHighScores(): Record<number, number> {\n  try {\n    const stored = localStorage.getItem(HIGH_SCORE_STORAGE_KEY)\n    if (stored) {\n      return JSON.parse(stored)\n    }\n  } catch (e) {\n    console.warn('Failed to load high scores from localStorage:', e)\n  }\n  return {}\n}\n\nfunction saveHighScores(scores: Record<number, number>): void {\n  try {\n    localStorage.setItem(HIGH_SCORE_STORAGE_KEY, JSON.stringify(scores))\n  } catch (e) {\n    console.warn('Failed to save high scores to localStorage:', e)\n  }\n}\n```\n- Try-catch with warning logs\n- No retry mechanism\n- Falls back to default values on failure\n\n---\n\n## What's MISSING\n\n### Retry Mechanisms\n- No exponential backoff implementation\n- No configurable retry attempts (maxRetries)\n- No retry delay functions\n- No retry utility modules\n- No retry for AudioContext initialization\n- No retry for canvas operations\n\n### Advanced Retry Patterns\n- No circuit breaker pattern\n- No exponential backoff with jitter\n- No timeout-based retry limits\n- No retry with backoff caps\n- No retry for specific error types only\n\n### Network Operations\n- No network calls in the application (client-side only)\n- No retry libraries (no retry-axios, no exponential-backoff, etc.)\n- No polling or watch mechanisms\n\n### Other Patterns\n- No resilience patterns\n- No reconnection logic\n- No recovery strategies beyond basic try-catch\n- No error classification for retryable vs non-retryable errors\n\n---\n\n## Dependencies Check\n\nFrom `package.json`, no retry-related libraries are installed:\n- Only React and React DOM as dependencies\n- No `retry`, `async-retry`, `exponential-backoff`, or similar packages\n- No third-party retry utilities\n\n---\n\n## Recommendations\n\nIf retry mechanisms are needed, consider implementing:\n\n1. **Retry utility with exponential backoff:**\n```typescript\n// Example pattern that's NOT implemented\nasync function retryWithBackoff<T>(\n  fn: () => Promise<T>,\n  options: { maxAttempts: number; baseDelay: number }\n): Promise<T> {\n  let lastError\n  for (let attempt = 0; attempt < options.maxAttempts; attempt++) {\n    try {\n      return await fn()\n    } catch (error) {\n      lastError = error\n      const delay = Math.pow(2, attempt) * options.baseDelay\n      await new Promise(resolve => setTimeout(resolve, delay))\n    }\n  }\n  throw lastError\n}\n```\n\n2. **Configurable retry attempts for localStorage operations**\n3. **Retry for AudioContext initialization**\n4. **Circuit breaker pattern for critical operations**\n\nThe current implementation has basic error handling with graceful degradation but lacks sophisticated retry mechanisms with exponential backoff.\n</task_result>","title":"Verify retry mechanisms implementation","metadata":{"sessionId":"ses_39a46