in(elapsed / animation.duration, 1)\n  const easeProgress = 1 - Math.pow(1 - progress, 3)  // Why cubic ease-out?\n  // ...\n}\n```\n\n---\n\n### Positive Findings\n\n**One area with some documentation:**\n\n**`/home/ochanomizu/repos/game_of_life/src/lib/presets.ts`** (lines 149-157):\n```typescript\nexport function getPresetDescription(preset: Preset): string {\n  const descriptions: Record<Preset, string> = {\n    EASY: 'Generous resources and time limits for a relaxed experience',\n    NORMAL: 'Balanced gameplay for standard challenge',\n    HARD: 'Strict resources and shorter time limits for experienced players',\n    CHAOS: 'Extreme settings with rapid changes and high scoring potential',\n  }\n  return descriptions[preset]\n}\n```\nThis provides user-facing descriptions, but not technical documentation.\n\n---\n\n### Recommendations\n\n1. **Add JSDoc/TSDoc comments** to all exported functions\n2. **Document complex algorithms** with inline comments explaining the \"why\" not just \"what\"\n3. **Add comments for state machine logic** explaining valid transitions and state invariants\n4. **Document performance-critical sections** with notes on optimization strategies\n5. **Add type documentation** explaining the purpose and constraints of each interface\n6. **Consider using a linter** to enforce documentation coverage (e.g., eslint-plugin-jsdoc)\n\n---\n\n### Conclusion\n\nThe codebase has a **critical documentation gap**. While the code appears well-structured and follows TypeScript best practices, the complete lack of documentation makes it:\n- Difficult for new developers to understand\n- Hard to maintain without intimate knowledge\n- Challenging to extend without studying implementation details\n- Lacking in API discoverability\n\n**Documentation Coverage: < 0.1%**\n</task_result>","title":"Verify code documentation","metadata":{"sessionId":"ses_39a465966ffefR2fot53UUwRJy","model":{"modelID":"glm-4.7","providerID":"zai-coding-plan"},"truncated":false},"time"