{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1771233464938,"sessionID":"ses_39a498265ffe1RQFH24Zh3M3iW","part":{"id":"prt_c65b9a64c001r1r691Szw7fU6o","sessionID":"ses_39a498265ffe1RQFH24Zh3M3iW","messageID":"msg_c65b8e3dd001sjt0S18svT5XWa","type":"tool","callID":"call_b5abaeea65dc439c81727cde","tool":"task","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"description":"Verify screen reader support","prompt":"Search /home/ochanomizu/repos/game_of_life/src for accessibility and ARIA attributes. Look for:\n1. ARIA labels on UI elements\n2. Live regions for score/timer updates\n3. Alternative text for visual elements\n4. Screen reader announcements for game state changes\n5. Any accessibility-specific attributes\n\nReturn findings about what accessibility features are implemented and what's missing.","subagent_type":"explore"},"output":"task_id: ses_39a4659a8ffeNIxyiLK8fbDZIS (for resuming to continue this task if needed)\n\n<task_result>\nBased on my comprehensive search of the `/home/ochanomizu/repos/game_of_life/src` directory, here are my findings about accessibility and ARIA attributes:\n\n## Accessibility Features Currently Implemented\n\n### 1. ARIA Labels\n**Found:** 1 instance\n- **UIToggleButton.tsx (line 13):** `aria-label` on the UI toggle button showing \"Hide UI\" or \"Show UI\" based on current state\n\n### 2. Form Accessibility\n**Found:** 19 label-input associations using `htmlFor` and `id`\n- All form controls in SettingsPanel.tsx are properly labeled:\n  - Difficulty Preset select\n  - Audio settings (enable checkbox, volume slider, waveform select)\n  - Movement Detection sliders (history, threshold, min size)\n  - Scoring settings sliders\n  - Level Generation settings (time, flux, difficulty mode)\n  - Grid Sizing settings (mobile, desktop cell size)\n  - Danger Zone settings (chaos multiplier, timer speed)\n  - High Contrast Mode checkbox\n\n### 3. Keyboard Navigation\n**Implemented:**\n- **Transition skipping:** Space and ESC keys skip level transition overlays (useTransition.ts lines 90-96)\n- **Settings toggle:** Backquote (`) key opens/closes settings panel (Game.tsx lines 98-106)\n- **Grid toggle:** G key toggles grid lines (Game.tsx lines 103-106)\n- **Proper event handling:** `preventDefault()` used appropriately to prevent unintended behaviors\n\n### 4. Semantic HTML Structure\n**Found:** 22 heading elements\n- Proper heading hierarchy (h1, h2, h3):\n  - Game title: `<h1>` \"Level X - Conway's Game of Life\" (Game.tsx line 407)\n  - Victory: `<h1>` \"VICTORY\" (VictoryScreen.tsx)\n  - Intro: `<h1>` \"CONWAY'S GAME OF LIFE\" (IntroOverlay.tsx)\n  - Error: `<h1>` \"Something went wrong\" (ErrorBoundary.tsx)\n  - Settings panel: `<h2>` \"Settings\" with multiple `<h3>` sections\n  - Stats sections: Multiple `<h3>` headings for Score, Time, Patterns, Stats (LevelStats.tsx)\n- `<section>` elements used for semantic grouping (SettingsPanel.tsx)\n\n### 5. Reduced Motion Support\n**Found:** CSS media query in index.css (lines 63-67)\n```css\n@media (prefers-reduced-motion: reduce) {\n  button {\n    transition: none;\n  }\n}\n```\n\n### 6. Accessibility Settings\n**Found:** High Contrast Mode option\n- Type definition in types/index.ts (line 114): `highContrastMode?: boolean`\n- SettingsPanel.tsx (lines 666-680): Accessibility section with High Contrast Mode toggle\n- Help text: \"Increases contrast and text size for improved readability and accessibility\"\n- Note: The CSS implementation for high contrast mode was **not found** in the styles\n\n### 7. HTML Metadata\n**Found in index.html:**\n- `lang=\"en\"` attribute on html element\n- Meta description: \"Conway's Game of Life - A strategic cellular automaton puzzle game\"\n- Page title: \"Conway's Game of Life\"\n\n## Critical Missing Accessibility Features\n\n### 1. Live Regions for Dynamic Content\n**Status:** Not implemented\n- ScoreDisplay.tsx: No `aria-live` region for score updates (changes frequently during gameplay)\n- FluxDisplay.tsx: No `aria-live` region for flux changes\n- GlassHUD.tsx: No `aria-live` for timer countdown, generation count, or alive cells\n- **Impact:** Screen reader users won't know when score, timer, or other game metrics change\n\n### 2. Screen Reader Announcements for Game State Changes\n**Status:** Not implemented\n- No announcements for:\n  - Level completion (\"Level X Complete\")\n  - Victory screen (\"VICTORY\")\n  - Phase changes (PLANNING → COUNTDOWN → RUNNING → FINISHED)\n  - New high score achievement\n  - Pattern type discoveries (movers, oscillators)\n  - Errors (insufficient flux)\n\n### 3. Canvas Accessibility\n**Status:** Minimal\n- CanvasGrid.tsx (lines 210-216): Canvas element has no:\n  - `aria-label` or `aria-labelledby`\n  - `role=\"application\"` or `role=\"grid\"`\n  - Fallback content for screen readers\n  - Alternative text describing the grid state\n  - Cell state information for screen readers\n- Only has `touchAction: 'none'` to prevent touch scrolling\n\n### 4. Button Accessibility\n**Status:** Missing ARIA labels on most buttons\n**Missing from:**\n- GlassHUD.tsx:\n  - STEP button (line 63)\n  - START/RUNNING button (line 70)\n  - RANDOM button (line 73)\n  - CLEAR button (line 80)\n  - DRAW button (line 90)\n  - ERASE button (line 97)\n  - Grid toggle button (line 127)\n  - Settings gear icon button (line 130, emoji-only)\n- VictoryScreen.tsx: Play Again button (line 53)\n- IntroOverlay.tsx: ENTER VOID button (lines 18, 27)\n- ErrorBoundary.tsx: Reload Page button (line 58)\n- SettingsPanel.tsx: Close button (line 290, \"×\" character only)\n\n**Note:** While these buttons have visible text, adding `aria-label` provides redundancy and can be clearer for screen readers, especially for emoji or icon-only buttons.\n\n### 5. Additional ARIA Attributes\n**Status:** None found\n- No `aria-hidden` on decorative elements\n- No `aria-describedby` for additional context\n- No `aria-expanded` on toggle elements (settings panel, UI toggle)\n- No `aria-pressed` on toggle buttons\n- No `aria-modal` on overlays (settings panel, victory screen)\n- No `aria-controls` relationships\n\n### 6. Focus Management\n**Status:** Not implemented\n- No focus traps in modals (settings panel, victory screen)\n- No focus restoration after closing overlays\n- No visible focus indicators in CSS\n- No `onFocus` or `onBlur` handlers for focus management\n- Initial focus not set when overlays open\n\n### 7. Alternative Text for Visual Elements\n**Status:** No images found in codebase, so no alt attributes needed\n- No `<img>` elements were found in the search\n\n### 8. Skip Navigation\n**Status:** Not implemented\n- No skip-to-content link\n- No skip-to-main link\n- No skip-navigation mechanism\n\n### 9. Keyboard Navigation Order\n**Status:** Not explicitly managed\n- No `tabindex` attributes found\n- No explicit tab order management\n- No keyboard shortcuts documented for main gameplay controls\n\n### 10. Error Messages\n**Status:** Partially accessible\n- ErrorBoundary.tsx has error messages with heading elements\n- No `role=\"alert\"` or `aria-live=\"assertive\"` for error announcements\n- Settings import errors (line 211) displayed as text but not announced\n\n## Summary\n\n**Strengths:**\n- Proper form labeling in settings\n- Semantic heading structure\n- Keyboard shortcuts for some actions\n- Reduced motion CSS support\n- High contrast mode setting (though CSS implementation is missing)\n\n**Major Gaps:**\n- No live regions for dynamic game updates (score, timer, flux)\n- No screen reader announcements for game state changes\n- Canvas element lacks accessibility attributes and fallback content\n- Most buttons lack ARIA labels for clarity\n- No focus management in overlays\n- High contrast mode setting exists but CSS implementation is missing\n- No skip navigation links\n- No modal or dialog roles for overlays\n\n**Recommendations Priority:**\n1. Add `aria-live` regions for score, timer, and flux updates\n2. Add canvas accessibility (role, label, or fallback content)\n3. Add ARIA labels to buttons, especially icon-only ones\n4. Implement focus management for modals\n5. Add screen reader announcements for game state changes\n6. Add CSS implementation for high contrast mode\n7. Consider adding skip navigation link\n8. Add `aria-live` for error messages\n</task_result>","title":"Verify screen reader support","metadata":{"sessionId":"ses_39a4659a8ffeNIxyiLK8fbDZIS","model":{"modelID":"glm-4.7","providerID":"zai-coding-plan"},"truncated":false},"time":{"start":1771233191509,"end":1771233464936}}}}
