oss entire codebase\n1433: - Files updated: VictoryScreen.css, IntroOverlay.css, TransitionOverlay.css, SettingsPanel.css, GlassHUD.css, ScoreDisplay.css, LevelStats.css, FluxDisplay.css, index.css, ErrorBoundary.css\n1434: - Prioritized disabling infinite animations (glitch, pulse-glow, pulse) as they cause most vestibular issues\n1435: - Simplified visual feedback for users with motion sensitivity by removing all motion\n1436: - All 364 tests passing with reduced motion support enabled\n1437: \n1438: **Technical Decisions:**\n1439: \n1440: - Used CSS @media (prefers-reduced-motion: reduce) query to detect user's motion preference\n1441: - Set animation: none and transition: none for all animated elements when reduced motion is preferred\n1442: - Set transform: none for hover/active states to prevent scale animations\n1443: - Applied overrides at end of each CSS file to ensure they take precedence\n1444: - Maintains full functionality while removing all motion effects\n1445: - Respects OS-level accessibility settings for users with vestibular disorders or motion sensitivity\n1446: \n1447: ### 6.3 Performance Optimization (LOW - Performance)\n\n(File has more lines. Use 'offset' parameter to read beyond line 1447)\n</content>","title":"IMPLEMENTATION_PLAN.md","metadata":{"preview":"### 6.2 Accessibility (LOW - Inclusivity)\n\n- [ ] Implement keyboard navigation\n  - Arrow keys for grid navigation\n  - Enter/Space to place cells\n  - Escape to cancel/close panels\n  - Tab navigation through UI controls\n- [ ] Add screen reader support\n  - ARIA labels for UI elements\n  - Announce game state changes\n  - Alternative text for visual elements\n  - Live regions for score/timer updates\n- [x] Implement reduced motion support\n  - Respect prefers-reduced-motion media query\n  - Disable animations when requested\n  - Simplified visual feedback\n- [ ] Add high contrast mode\n  - Toggle for high contrast colors\n  - Larger text option\n  - Improved readability","truncated":t